SC-598 r2 mutants (identity I1). Source under test: dse 47950f45 (fix 3befe3ff + test fb1761ba; managedModal.ts identical to the version reviewed at fix). Runner: sc598-r2-mutate.py.txt (scratch copy). Each mutant edits one source file, runs jest on the named suites
(managedModal.test.ts, stamina-bar.test.ts, montage.test.ts; SC-597 mutants only the opener's own suite, K6 both), then restores with 'git checkout HEAD -- <file>' and asserts 'git diff --stat' is empty.
N1-N17 (19 with the a/b variants) = SC-598 mutants of managedModal.ts; K1-K6 and G1-G6 (x2 openers) = the 23 SC-597 mutants of sc597-r2-mutants.log re-run against the UPDATED SC-597 tests.
Result: N 19/19 killed (N1, N2, N3a, N3b, N4a, N4b, N5-N17) (N16 and N17 first SURVIVED/crashed-unnamed at fb1761ba's parent, which is why the commit adds `cancelable` and `view` assertions; the entries below for N16/N17 are the re-runs on fb1761ba), SC-597 23/23 killed. 42/42.
The N17 entry's red is 'Test suite failed to run': without `view` jsdom throws "Cannot read properties of null (reading '_location')" in an uncaught handler and the managedModal suite does not load; with the crash filtered out the new `expect(clicks[1].view).toBe(window)` kills it as well (checked by hand: 1 failed, 61 passed on managedModal.test.ts alone).
The first-pass entries of N16 and N17 (before the `cancelable` / `view` assertions existed; N17's is the runner mislabelling a crashed suite as SURVIVED) stay below, followed by their re-runs.

